<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Trans Hex lifts year share, ups div.</title>
<headline>Trans Hex lifts year share, ups div.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1996-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr before except</p>
<p>    items  (cts)	     374.8	vs  268.0</p>
<p>Shr after except</p>
<p>    items (cts)		393.5	vs  255.3</p>
<p>    Total div (cts)	  105.0	vs  81.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    59.29	vs  38.47</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    85.91	vs  63.43</p>
<p>    Tax			  28.86	vs  23.36</p>
<p>    Interest paid	     1.58	vs  1.07</p>
<p>    Diamond turnover	227.48	vs  171.82</p>
<p>    Lime turnover	    33.85	vs  32.09</p>
<p>    Exceptionals received  3.63	 vs  3.05 paid</p>
<p>Div payable July 4</p>
<p>on register June 20</p>
<p>Full name: Trans Hex Group Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said it expected continued high earnings in the current year despite large amounts due to be spent on exploration.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
